---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
---

<Base title="University Course" description="An official RWTH Aachen university course on effective altruism, featuring talks from world-leading experts.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Project Leonardo"
    title="University course"
    lead="In cooperation with RWTH Aachen University, EA Aachen offers an official course on effective altruism — featuring talks from world-leading experts in academia and the philanthropic sector."
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
    <Prose>
      <p>
        <a href="http://eepurl.com/g5LGrL">Subscribe to our newsletter</a> to find out what we're offering — especially
        if you're an RWTH student.
      </p>

      <h2>Course summary</h2>
      <p>
        The overarching goal is to convey scientifically grounded ideas and methods you can apply in your own life to do
        good more effectively. Speakers research how to mitigate climate change or prevent global pandemics; others have
        founded internationally operating charities and share the insights they gained working directly on saving lives.
        The course is part of <a href="https://www.leonardo.rwth-aachen.de/en/homepage/">Project Leonardo</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Programme</h2>
      <p>For a sense of the format, here's a past course overview:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>"Effective Altruism" — an introduction · EA Aachen e.V.</li>
        <li>Global Health · Bruce Tsai, <a href="https://rethinkpriorities.org/">Rethink Priorities</a></li>
        <li>Farmed Animal Welfare · Jamie Harris, <a href="https://www.animaladvocacycareers.org/">Animal Advocacy Careers</a></li>
        <li>Summary "Neartermism" and introduction to "Longtermism" · EA Aachen e.V.</li>
        <li>Biorisk · Crystal Watson, <a href="https://www.centerforhealthsecurity.org/">Johns Hopkins Center for Health Security</a></li>
        <li>AI Safety · Tom Lieberum, AI safety researcher</li>
        <li>Summary "Longtermism" and criticism of effective altruism · EA Aachen e.V. & Prof. Kellerwessel</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>How to participate</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>RWTH students:</strong> register via RWTHonline. Depending on your course of study, you may be eligible for credit points.</li>
        <li><strong>External participants:</strong> just send a quick email to <a href="mailto:info@ea-aachen.org">info@ea-aachen.org</a> and you're ready to join.</li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>
  </section>
</Base>
